    "created_at": "2019-08-20T18:10:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-20T19:48:27Z",
    "body": "Unfortunately, I have a few concerns about adding this module to the prompt.\r\n1. Both TypeScript and Node share the same runtime. In addition to the `package` module, this will make the prompt even longer in TS projects.\r\n2. Often-times, TS is a versioned dependency. The locally installed version doesn't have much bearing on the project's development.\r\n3. `tsc --version` starts up a Node application, which unfortunately have slow cold-start times, that can noticeably affect the speed of the prompt:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4658208/63372165-9326b480-c353-11e9-883e-7ff2b0eb2d7b.png)\r\n\r\nI'd love to hear more about your use case, and perhaps find out how we can address these concerns.\r\n\r\nSolutions for 2 and 3 are to check `devDependencies.typescript` within `package.json` to retrieve the package version. \r\n\r\nAs a daily user of TypeScript, the version of TypeScript has a negligible effect on the way I program. I'm not sure it's worth the perceived added noise to add this module.",
